                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf8d73f3-fe54-376d-b803-f0b4e67dc867",
                                        "entry_id": "c1dbd985-9064-37f5-b51d-f21099773ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To furnish with barbs, or with that which will hold or hurt like barbs, as an arrow, fishhook, spear, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2af548f6-a5ea-481b-a690-b3753be934a9",
                                                "sense_id": "bf8d73f3-fe54-376d-b803-f0b4e67dc867",
                                                "text": "[…] for this day will pour down, / If I conjecture aught, no drizzling shower, / But rattling storm of arrows barbed with fire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f5019a7-4fd0-40aa-a59b-d6884598c898",
                                                "sense_id": "bf8d73f3-fe54-376d-b803-f0b4e67dc867",
                                                "text": "Undoubtedly—when Ingratitude barbs the Dart of Injury—the wound has double danger in it—"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae83ec5f-985a-4ce7-aad8-4d02105eac09",
                                                "sense_id": "bf8d73f3-fe54-376d-b803-f0b4e67dc867",
                                                "text": "Orion hit a rabbit once; but though sore wounded it got to the bury, and, struggling in, the arrow caught the side of the hole and was drawn out. Indeed, a nail filed sharp is not of much avail as an arrowhead; you must have it barbed, and that was a little beyond our skill."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3fa0596-446a-4d11-84b4-89c25a7fe382",
                                                "sense_id": "bf8d73f3-fe54-376d-b803-f0b4e67dc867",
                                                "text": "Her coat was a tangled mass, barbed with last year's burs, matted disgustingly with cow dung."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ea333c1-ec09-35b6-ba3b-e9b1167765b5",
                                        "entry_id": "c1dbd985-9064-37f5-b51d-f21099773ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut (hair)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Nigeria"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f406391-a191-3def-b4ae-44e834a87d44",
                                        "entry_id": "c1dbd985-9064-37f5-b51d-f21099773ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shave or dress the beard of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffcea4b9-dcab-32c2-8dde-942ae9de4066",
                                        "entry_id": "c1dbd985-9064-37f5-b51d-f21099773ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To clip; to mow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0db5ca3-f971-4471-9a67-87666c2d5113",
                                                "sense_id": "ffcea4b9-dcab-32c2-8dde-942ae9de4066",
                                                "text": "O thou pale ſober night, / […] / The ſtooping Sitheman that dooth barbe the field, / Thou makſt winke ſure: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "barb",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17a1020a-f730-33a3-be39-e1593ebac16f",
                                        "entry_id": "4def7c09-f22f-3686-b916-d4aa8fcd893d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Barbary horse, a superior breed introduced from Barbary into Spain by the Moors."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "716e0fa8-9082-48be-8db2-3143ae3f9f0f",
                                                "sense_id": "17a1020a-f730-33a3-be39-e1593ebac16f",
                                                "text": "Why sends not the Bridegroom his promised gift, / Is his heart more cold, or his barb less swift?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e33e0711-a9ab-4d4c-a126-22a238c3a8b1",
                                                "sense_id": "17a1020a-f730-33a3-be39-e1593ebac16f",
                                                "text": "However, in the last few years, the stud farms in Morocco and elsewhere in the world have rediscovered the qualities of the barb, which, in Berber tradition, remains the king of the \"fantasias\", a festival that is also becoming fashionable once again.",
                                                "translation": "In the Kingdom of the Horse: The National Studs of Morocco",
                                                "english": "In the Kingdom of the Horse: The National Studs of Morocco"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d41d927b-d22d-356f-835a-766049b4f349",
                                        "entry_id": "4def7c09-f22f-3686-b916-d4aa8fcd893d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A blackish or dun variety of pigeon, originally brought from Barbary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
